---
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro";
import CaseSection from "../../components/CaseSection.astro";
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex";
import { caseStudyStyles } from "../../styles/caseStudyStyles";
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Medical Imaging Pipeline | Warre Snaet"
  description="A clinical imaging pipeline Warre Snaet built during an international internship at 2Ai IPCA in Barcelos, Portugal."
  kicker="International internship · Feb–Jun 2026"
  heading="Medical imaging pipeline"
  lead="A Python pipeline that reads the measurements embedded in echocardiographic studies and turns them into structured research data that a person can review."
  meta={[
    { label: "My role", value: "AI & software engineering intern" },
    { label: "Stack", value: "Python, DICOM, OpenCV, OCR, image processing" },
    { label: "Context", value: "2Ai IPCA · Barcelos, Portugal" },
  ]}
>
  <CaseSection label="Problem" title="Measurements stuck inside images">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>The measurements the research needed were burned into the echocardiographic images instead of being stored as separate fields. Copying them out by hand was slow, hard to repeat, and hard to check across large batches of studies.</p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Pipeline" title="Detection, extraction, and review">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Read echocardiographic DICOM studies and found the regions that contain burned-in measurements.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Combined OCR and image processing to extract the values and export them as normalized JSON.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Made batch processing resumable, so a long run can pick up where it left off after an interruption.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Added validation queues and review tools so a person can see and check any output the pipeline is unsure about.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}>Extracted ECG traces for later analysis.</li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Optimization" title="Check the metadata before matching images">
    <p {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.paragraph)}>I wrote a source-video matcher that uses DICOM metadata and OpenCV ECC alignment. Filtering on metadata first leaves far fewer candidates to align, which brought one representative run down from roughly 21 hours to 23 minutes.</p>
  </CaseSection>

  <CaseSection label="Engineering" title="Reliable enough for research work">
    <ul {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.list, caseStudyStyles.factsList)}>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Resumable work</strong>Saved intermediate state means an interrupted batch doesn't start over from zero.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Human validation</strong>Uncertain extractions go to a review queue, separate from accepted output.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Traceable output</strong>The structured exports record which source study each extracted value came from.</li>
      <li {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.listItem)}><strong {...stylex.attrs(caseStudyStyles.emphasizedFact)}>Practical handoff</strong>Documentation for each platform lets other people run the pipeline on their own machines, not just mine.</li>
    </ul>
  </CaseSection>
</CaseStudyLayout>
